# Paper B Scope Boundary — Material to Treat as Prior/Imported in the New Paper

The separate manuscript **Operator-Level Boolean Computation with Correspondence Matrices** should receive its own credit/citation and should not be cannibalized as novelty of the new rotation/modal paper.

Treat the following as Paper-B material unless the new paper proves a materially stronger extension:

- binary 2x2 CM representation of a Boolean connective;
- declared operand frames / truth-state ordering;
- XOR–AND row-by-column contraction;
- coefficient-space linearity versus input-function linearity;
- operand exchange by transpose;
- row/column input-polarity transformations;
- entrywise output complement;
- frame alignment and sound same-frame pointwise operator fusion;
- operator-on-operator Boolean computation within aligned frames;
- compiler/folding interpretation and fallback boundaries;
- formula-valued Logical Matrices (LMs);
- positive valuation from LM to CM;
- valuation commuting with Boolean operations and LM pairing;
- logical-pairing / measurement-like LM contraction;
- distinction from ANF coefficients and STP logical structure matrices;
- benchmarking/evidence boundaries for compiler speedups.

The new paper can cite these as the logical substrate and then ask what happens when **geometric rotation of the four CM coefficient positions is lifted into an operator action on coefficient space**.

Recommended transition sentence for a future paper:

> Building on the typed Boolean operator calculus and symbolic LM/CM correspondence developed previously, we now promote the geometric four-cycle of the CM coefficient positions to an explicit Boolean-linear operator and study the algebra, semantic correspondences, and restricted modal theory induced by that lift.
